From f80ef118ccacde6be891bdaa354f6a32212dc009 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: onlyfish <linotfish@outlook.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 16:56:41 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] audioflinger: keep all daxService HIDL traffic off the
 audio locks

EffectDapDmsClient::connect() (tryGetService, linkToDeath, registerClient and
three getIntParam calls) and disconnect() (unregisterClient) ran synchronously
from callers that hold AudioFlinger_Mutex/ThreadBase_Mutex/EffectChain_Mutex:
createEffect() and moveEffectChain_ll() both call onGlobalMixChainAttached()
inside their lock scopes, and EffectChain::removeEffect() calls effectReleased()
with the chain lock held. A slow or restarting daxService therefore stalled the
whole audio framework.

- Run every DMS connect/disconnect on a private worker thread; callers only
  queue a request.
- Fix the controller/DMS lock inversion: the Dolby state callback used to run
  inside EffectDapDmsClient::mLock while taking the controller lock, while
  effectReleased() took the controller lock and then the DMS lock.
- Reconnect when the DMS service dies, with 1s backoff capped at 30 attempts,
  instead of staying disconnected until the DAP effect is recreated.
- Routing-invalidate worker: make the AudioFlinger pointer atomic, start the
  thread joinable, interrupt the sleeps with a timed cond wait, and join before
  AudioFlinger is destroyed.
- Join the property watcher in destroy() and detach the HIDL callbacks before
  the controller is deleted.
- Query the isUpmixSupportedPkg HAL value only when the playing package changes.
- Skip mLock in runPendingDapPregainOnMixThread() unless a restart was queued.
- Make EffectModule::mSkipEffectProcess atomic (written by binder threads, read
  by the mixer thread) and stop logging the arbitration result when it did not
  change. Negative-cache the app whitelist XML read.

